// expect: 134
// SYNTAX §Indexing: bounds-checking is RUNTIME for lists — traps on
// out-of-range. This fixture is the law's executable form: xs[99] on a
// three-element list must TRAP (exit 134), never read adjacent memory.
// Before 2026-07-18 the tag-0 read was raw and this program returned
// whatever word sat past the list — the silent-wrong the checked
// list_index deleted. The index arrives through a parameter, so nothing
// at the read proves or refutes its bounds and the read is the checked one;
// a constant index past a literal is refuted before it runs (TRAP,
// 2026-10-06 — tests/crown/leak-claim-index-past-literal.mn).
fn at(xs, i) = xs[i]

fn main() = at([10, 20, 30], 99)
